 # Bank Data Analysis Project


##  Overview
-This project focuses on Bank Analytics, where I analyzed real-world banking datasets to uncover patterns in loans, customer behavior, and branch performance. Using Excel, Power BI and MySQL, I created interactive dashboards and SQL-driven insights to support data-driven banking decisions.
Objectives
-Clean and preprocess raw banking datasets.
-Build interactive dashboards for loan analytics & customer trends.
-Write SQL queries to extract key financial metrics.
-Provide actionable business insights for better decision-making.

## Tools & Technologies

-Excel → Pivot tables, charts, KPI dashboards

-Power BI & Tableau → DAX measures, advanced visuals, interactive dashboards

-MySQL → Data extraction, aggregation & query-driven insights

## Dataset Used

-Customer demographics (Age, Region, Branch, Religion)

-Loan details (Amount, Funded amount, Interest, Status, Repayment)

-Branch-level & State-level financial performance

##  Dashboards & Visuals

✅ Loan demand & disbursement patterns
✅ Customer segmentation & repayment trends
✅ Branch & State-level loan performance
✅ Identification of delinquent & default loan risks

##  Key Insights

- Loan Demand: Higher among working-age customers (business & personal purposes).
- Branch Performance: Some branches have strong credit inflows, while others face more defaults.
- Regional Trends: Maximum disbursement observed in Uttar Pradesh, Punjab, and Haryana.
- Risk Factors: Noticeable delinquency in certain loan categories → need for stricter verification.

## Challenges

- Data cleaning (duplicates, missing values, inconsistent formats).
-Defining KPIs that translate raw financial data into meaningful metrics.
- Balancing dashboard detail with simplicity for decision-making.
- SQL query errors due to incomplete data loading (fixed via reprocessing).

## Conclusion

The Bank Analytics Dashboard gives a holistic view of customer behavior and loan performance. It highlights:

- Who demands loans most

- Where loans are concentrated

- How repayment patterns differ across segments

- What risks banks must address
